<title>UK: Fannie Mae sets 10 bln yen dual-currency bond.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae sets 10 bln yen dual-currency bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Merrill Lynch and Wako International Europe.</p>
<p> BORROWER   FANNIE MAE</p>
<p> AMT    10 BLN YEN    COUPON     5.12	MATURITY    28.JUN.99</p>
<p> TYPE   DUAL-CURRENCY ISS PRICE  PAR	 PAY DATE  L-27.JUN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.50	DENOMS (K) 500	 LISTING     NONE</p>
<p> PAY FREQ   SEMI ANN  SALE LIMITS US/JP    FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> NOTES	REDEMPTION IS AT $4,299.23 PER 500,000 YEN BOND</p>
<p>		L-LONG FIRST COUPON</p>
<p>		ISSUED UNDER GLOBAL DEBT FACILITY</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
